1
00:01:40,879 --> 00:01:42,719
Still trying to crack Lin Kanshan's email password?

2
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:43,959
Both SIM cards are encrypted.

3
00:01:44,239 --> 00:01:45,480
Can't crack them anytime soon.

4
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,079
I can only try my luck with his email.

5
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:48,560
What about you?

6
00:01:48,879 --> 00:01:50,040
What's on your mind?

7
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,280
You suspect someone,

8
00:01:53,719 --> 00:01:55,400
but they've never suspected you.

9
00:01:55,719 --> 00:01:56,319
Right?

10
00:02:11,039 --> 00:02:12,840
Tell me, the two of us staying here every day,

11
00:02:14,879 --> 00:02:15,800
what's the point?

12
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:17,439
Who knows if Lin Kanshan

13
00:02:17,439 --> 00:02:19,199
will even come back tonight?

14
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,919
Who knows if anyone will come looking for him?

15
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:24,319
All we can do is sit here and wait.

16
00:02:25,879 --> 00:02:27,520
If he doesn't come back for ten years,

17
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:30,120
will we have to wait here for ten years?

18
00:02:30,919 --> 00:02:31,840
Wait until we retire,

19
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,240
still trying to crack codes

20
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:34,680
that might already be obsolete?

21
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,599
The last time

22
00:02:45,599 --> 00:02:47,560
I went to eat at the cafeteria,

23
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:50,159
I ran into Old Liu from Tech.

24
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:52,560
He rushed through his meal,

25
00:02:53,159 --> 00:02:54,599
having tests to run right after.

26
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:56,879
He was under so much stress.

27
00:02:57,680 --> 00:02:59,560
Whether handling a crisis or making arrests,

28
00:03:00,199 --> 00:03:01,520
like the return of Hong Kong, China,

29
00:03:02,319 --> 00:03:03,719
when hostile foreign forces infiltrated,

30
00:03:04,879 --> 00:03:06,400
we never knew where they hid.

31
00:03:07,319 --> 00:03:08,800
Every time was a race against the clock,

32
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:11,159
always requiring him to find them

33
00:03:11,159 --> 00:03:12,479
within the deadline.

34
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,919
Living with that stress day in and day out,

35
00:03:17,599 --> 00:03:19,159
with his heart constantly racing,

36
00:03:19,159 --> 00:03:20,680
how could his heart stay healthy?

37
00:03:23,319 --> 00:03:24,960
I'm afraid I'll end up like that too.

38
00:03:28,719 --> 00:03:30,719
Cao Liaoping was my first case.

39
00:03:33,199 --> 00:03:35,400
The first thing I did every morning was tail him.

40
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,560
I didn't know how long it would take,

41
00:03:38,879 --> 00:03:40,520
or if I'd follow him until retirement.

42
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:42,479
It was finally wrapped up.

43
00:03:43,039 --> 00:03:44,199
I brought him back.

44
00:03:45,879 --> 00:03:47,599
I remember that day so clearly.

45
00:03:48,639 --> 00:03:51,240
The plane touched down at 10:23 p.m.

46
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:53,039
I didn't walk out until the early morning.

47
00:03:54,039 --> 00:03:55,680
Walking home along the city wall,

48
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,439
I saw a couple.

49
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:01,479
They were flying a kite.

50
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:06,199
The sky was full of stars,

51
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:08,639
peaceful and quiet.

52
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:15,719
That was the first time I felt

53
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:17,920
the sense of pride my job brings.

54
00:04:19,319 --> 00:04:21,000
Ordinary people live such good lives,

55
00:04:22,079 --> 00:04:23,439
and life can be enjoyed like that.

56
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:34,160
That was all earned through our

57
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,240
day-in, day-out monotonous work.

58
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:44,279
Does that sound a bit sentimental?

59
00:04:52,959 --> 00:04:54,319
You don't need to comfort me.

60
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:55,879
That's not what I mean.

61
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:00,920
What I mean is,

62
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:02,240
say you're a doctor.

63
00:05:03,199 --> 00:05:04,800
You perform a surgery today.

64
00:05:05,199 --> 00:05:06,600
Success or failure comes quickly.

65
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,879
But the work I do takes so long.

66
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:13,040
The sense of accomplishment comes so slowly.

67
00:05:13,439 --> 00:05:14,560
Decades of hard work,

68
00:05:15,279 --> 00:05:16,399
and your hair turns gray.

69
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:20,800
Now I have to psyche myself up every day.

70
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:23,759
I tell myself, "Yu Lixia,

71
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:26,519
Jinlan,

72
00:05:27,759 --> 00:05:29,480
you have to grit your teeth and hang in there.

73
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:32,040
Anyone else can say they quit,

74
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,240
but you can't.

75
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,800
Otherwise, who's going to take over?"

76
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:43,959
Forget about that.

77
00:05:44,639 --> 00:05:46,120
Tell me more about that rainy day,

78
00:05:46,519 --> 00:05:49,360
when you and your ex pushed your bikes home.

79
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,079
During the big earthquake that year,

80
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:54,120
her house was unsafe to live in.

81
00:05:55,079 --> 00:05:55,879
Some people...

82
00:05:58,040 --> 00:05:59,279
they're just gone in a flash.

83
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,160
I'm so sleepy.

84
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:32,560
Let's get some sleep.

85
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:13,519
Who is this?

86
00:07:13,519 --> 00:07:15,720
Municipal Economic Crimes Detachment. Officer He.

87
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:17,560
Badge 3953.

88
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:19,360
We have a financial fraud case,

89
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:21,600
regarding transfers made to overseas accounts.

90
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:23,040
We'd like to ask you a few questions.

91
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:23,720
Cooperate with our investigation.

92
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,199
Financial fraud?

93
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,000
You need me to cooperate?

94
00:07:27,199 --> 00:07:27,920
In person?

95
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:29,720
Yes, in person.

96
00:07:33,959 --> 00:07:34,680
I see.

97
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:37,759
Give me an hour, then.

98
00:07:38,639 --> 00:07:40,360
Meet me at East Asia Garment Factory.

99
00:07:40,839 --> 00:07:42,879
Fine. We'll come to your office.

100
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:45,120
Brother Qi.

101
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,600
Boss Ding has seen us before.

102
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:47,920
He knows we're with Lin Kanshan,

103
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:49,680
leasing medical equipment.

104
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,480
If we just go see him like this,

105
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:53,160
won't he start blabbing?

106
00:07:53,279 --> 00:07:54,399
Keep the case quiet,

107
00:07:54,399 --> 00:07:55,680
and all is peaceful.

108
00:07:55,879 --> 00:07:57,639
If he can't keep his mouth shut,

109
00:07:57,879 --> 00:07:59,199
he's finished around here.

110
00:07:59,199 --> 00:08:01,120
Relax. As long as you have authority,

111
00:08:01,319 --> 00:08:02,120
you won't find anyone

112
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:04,079
tighter-lipped than an entrepreneur.

113
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:05,639
Keep eyes on Wen Zongshu,

114
00:08:05,639 --> 00:08:07,240
crack Boss Ding first,

115
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:08,560
and circle in from the outside.

116
00:08:08,759 --> 00:08:10,240
That's an offensive mindset too, huh?

117
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,120
That's basic awareness.

118
00:08:16,399 --> 00:08:16,920
Morning, Brother Qi.

119
00:08:17,319 --> 00:08:17,759
Morning.

120
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:36,679
Boss Ding.

121
00:08:36,679 --> 00:08:38,320
We're already at the gate. Where are you?

122
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:40,440
So sorry, Officer He.

123
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:42,279
My car broke down on the way.

124
00:08:42,559 --> 00:08:44,320
I'm still on the highway at the foot of the hill.

125
00:08:45,039 --> 00:08:46,519
Then what time can you get here?

126
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:50,879
This afternoon... Probably around three.

127
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:52,399
All right.

128
00:08:53,639 --> 00:08:55,759
Brother Qi, he said his car broke down on the highway.

129
00:08:55,759 --> 00:08:56,960
He won't make it until three in the afternoon.

130
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,120
Pretty sly.

131
00:08:58,679 --> 00:09:01,080
Do you think he's been scammed before

132
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,519
and suspects we're scammers too?

133
00:09:02,639 --> 00:09:03,519
Want to bet?

134
00:09:04,159 --> 00:09:05,679
He might be right nearby,

135
00:09:05,679 --> 00:09:07,759
watching through binoculars to see who we are.

136
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:13,200
He won't meet with us.

137
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:14,240
Let's go.

138
00:09:15,879 --> 00:09:17,919
Boss, those two guys under the tree...

139
00:09:17,919 --> 00:09:19,679
look kind of familiar.

140
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:46,559
Wait.

141
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:47,840
It's the two of them.

142
00:09:52,559 --> 00:09:53,120
Brother Sun.

143
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:54,840
How did it go? Did you find anything?

144
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:55,919
I'm certain.

145
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:56,799
Yeah.

146
00:09:57,759 --> 00:10:00,679
Rong A-39530.

147
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:03,080
His plate is right in front of me now.

148
00:10:03,879 --> 00:10:05,200
A fake plate.

149
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:08,840
Thanks, Brother Sun.

150
00:10:09,159 --> 00:10:09,759
Okay, okay.

151
00:10:11,639 --> 00:10:13,480
Boss, should we call the police?

152
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:16,000
Someone from the chamber was kidnapped last month.

153
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,240
It was an inside job.

154
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:18,120
Impossible to guard against.

155
00:10:36,039 --> 00:10:38,440
The number you dialed is temporarily unavailable

156
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:39,440
or is powered off.

157
00:10:40,919 --> 00:10:41,559
It's turned off.

158
00:10:45,639 --> 00:10:47,080
Let's go to Technical Investigation.

159
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:48,399
Track his location.

160
00:10:53,679 --> 00:10:54,799
Don't let me find you.

161
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:09,440
I had Brother Li locate him using the latest tech,

162
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:11,279
and found Boss Ding's exact location.

163
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:14,039
It's two on two. What are our odds?

164
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:15,519
Should we head over?

165
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,879
Do you think he really planned to come here,

166
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:22,679
or did he deliberately lure us here?

167
00:11:22,759 --> 00:11:24,039
Nobody tipped him off.

168
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:25,960
How could he know we were tailing him?

169
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:29,279
In a place this remote,

170
00:11:29,399 --> 00:11:30,600
where even birds don't come to shit—

171
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,679
you think he wouldn't notice you showing up?

172
00:11:32,799 --> 00:11:34,200
So should we still go over?

173
00:11:34,399 --> 00:11:35,159
How about we make a call

174
00:11:35,159 --> 00:11:36,399
and bring in more backup?

175
00:11:37,879 --> 00:11:38,960
It's not a covert arrest.

176
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:40,279
Just assisting with an investigation.

177
00:11:40,279 --> 00:11:42,039
I doubt he'd dare bite my ass.

178
00:11:42,559 --> 00:11:43,240
Drive in.

179
00:12:10,639 --> 00:12:12,399
What do we do? Should we leave now?

180
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:13,480
This isn't a drug bust.

181
00:12:13,679 --> 00:12:14,679
It's not that serious.

182
00:12:14,879 --> 00:12:16,039
If a few guys like this scare us off,

183
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:17,200
we might as well quit.

184
00:12:17,759 --> 00:12:18,600
Don't get physical yet!

185
00:12:18,679 --> 00:12:20,000
We're undercover as police this time.

186
00:12:26,159 --> 00:12:26,840
Hit him!

187
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:29,600
You actually dared to make a move?

188
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:53,879
Nobody move!

189
00:12:54,799 --> 00:12:55,360
Police!

190
00:12:58,039 --> 00:12:58,799
Police!

191
00:12:59,639 --> 00:13:01,360
You dare hit a cop?

192
00:13:01,759 --> 00:13:03,240
You're really cops?

193
00:13:05,639 --> 00:13:07,559
Come on, let me give you a shot.

194
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:10,240
Stop whining. You're a grown man.

195
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:11,240
How was I supposed to know

196
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:12,960
real police would use fake plates?

197
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:14,039
Lately,

198
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:16,759
someone's always watching folks at the chamber.

199
00:13:16,759 --> 00:13:18,399
There've already been several kidnappings.

200
00:13:18,519 --> 00:13:19,240
Who wouldn't be scared?

201
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:20,639
Now I know.

202
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:22,679
Even the task force does business.

203
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:24,240
Strictly confidential.

204
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:27,519
You're very close to Wen Zongshu.

205
00:13:27,679 --> 00:13:28,519
How close, exactly?

206
00:13:28,759 --> 00:13:31,440
Close enough that we can borrow money from each other.

207
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:34,399
Is there something wrong with him?

208
00:13:37,039 --> 00:13:37,879
Starting today,

209
00:13:37,879 --> 00:13:38,879
I want to know the channels

210
00:13:38,879 --> 00:13:40,240
and methods he uses for cash flow.

211
00:13:40,399 --> 00:13:41,679
Including what he does every day.

212
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,159
Focus on anyone he meets more than twice.

213
00:13:44,679 --> 00:13:46,080
The more detail, the better.

214
00:13:49,279 --> 00:13:50,320
We won't let you help for nothing.

215
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:53,039
You can come to me with any trouble you have here.

216
00:13:54,919 --> 00:13:56,080
Any trouble? Like what, for example?

217
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:57,159
Like the night before last...

218
00:13:57,159 --> 00:13:58,639
going to Guangdong with Qian Xinfu.

219
00:13:58,799 --> 00:13:59,440
Got it.

220
00:14:00,519 --> 00:14:01,159
Consider it done.

221
00:14:12,519 --> 00:14:13,559
All right, keep walking.

222
00:14:13,679 --> 00:14:14,320
Straighten your leg a bit.

223
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:15,440
Step down firmly.

224
00:14:17,799 --> 00:14:18,919
Don't be afraid of the pain.

225
00:14:19,639 --> 00:14:21,399
Don't pull it back. Step down.

226
00:14:21,399 --> 00:14:22,759
Otherwise, it won't do any good.

227
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:23,639
Walk, walk, walk.

228
00:14:24,639 --> 00:14:25,519
Keep moving.

229
00:14:31,759 --> 00:14:32,759
Straighten your leg.

230
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:35,679
Don't always give up halfway.

231
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:36,519
The doctor said so.

232
00:14:36,679 --> 00:14:37,399
You have to walk.

233
00:14:37,399 --> 00:14:38,679
Otherwise, it's all for nothing.

234
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,440
I walk like this every day.

235
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:41,440
I just can't straighten it.

236
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:42,200
What do you want from me?

237
00:14:42,279 --> 00:14:43,600
Fine. Pull it back if it hurts.

238
00:14:43,759 --> 00:14:44,759
If you can't stand up later,

239
00:14:44,879 --> 00:14:45,840
that's on you.

240
00:14:46,279 --> 00:14:47,200
You ran off to the mainland

241
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:48,240
to live in luxury,

242
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:50,240
leaving me here all alone.

243
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:52,440
What am I supposed to do?

244
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:54,480
Don't bother with me.

245
00:14:57,879 --> 00:14:58,720
I don't need your help.

246
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:00,480
Get out.

247
00:15:00,639 --> 00:15:01,039
Come on.

248
00:15:01,039 --> 00:15:01,600
Get out!

249
00:15:01,799 --> 00:15:02,840
Don't be mad.

250
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:05,240
Aren't you going back to the mainland?

251
00:15:05,639 --> 00:15:06,279
Just go!

252
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,480
The older you get, the worse your temper gets.

253
00:15:10,799 --> 00:15:11,600
Leave me alone.

254
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:12,960
Getting angry won't do you any good.

255
00:15:13,919 --> 00:15:14,879
Stop nagging me.

256
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:16,320
With the Reform and Opening Up,

257
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:18,279
the mainland is full of money now.

258
00:15:18,919 --> 00:15:19,759
Making less means losing out.

259
00:15:19,759 --> 00:15:20,679
Don't you understand?

260
00:15:20,679 --> 00:15:21,759
If it weren't for you,

261
00:15:21,759 --> 00:15:22,799
I would've gone back yesterday.

262
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:24,480
What's the point of having a son?

263
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:25,600
Look at Old Yang next door.

264
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:26,440
He had a daughter.

265
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,480
The last caregiver complained

266
00:15:28,799 --> 00:15:29,799
that you groped her.

267
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,720
I brushed against her by accident!

268
00:15:32,159 --> 00:15:33,799
She had such a temper, why would I?

269
00:15:34,679 --> 00:15:36,039
You believe whatever she says.

270
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:37,399
What about the current one?

271
00:15:38,279 --> 00:15:39,360
Didn't you say you'd replace her?

272
00:15:39,679 --> 00:15:40,399
Now you won't.

273
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:42,120
Are you dating her or something?

274
00:15:42,519 --> 00:15:43,720
If you were a woman,

275
00:15:43,840 --> 00:15:45,039
would you date me?

276
00:15:47,440 --> 00:15:48,320
What about you?

277
00:15:48,919 --> 00:15:50,399
When are you getting married and having kids?

278
00:15:50,879 --> 00:15:52,559
I can barely take care of myself.

279
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:54,480
How would I have time for kids?

280
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,159
"Sons are useless," right?

281
00:15:56,159 --> 00:15:57,080
That's what you said.

282
00:15:58,440 --> 00:15:59,679
You won't even have a kid.

283
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,840
Who'll burn paper money when you die?

284
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,600
What about the ancestors and me?

285
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:04,799
That's why you should treat me better.

286
00:16:05,519 --> 00:16:07,080
Leave all your property to me,

287
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:09,320
and I'll start burning paper for you early.

288
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:10,159
Think of it as a prepayment.

289
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:13,440
What about your grandaunt?

290
00:16:14,279 --> 00:16:15,080
Still can't find her?

291
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:16,360
Still looking.

292
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:18,799
The mainland is huge. She's hard to find.

293
00:16:19,159 --> 00:16:20,720
It's just a small business.

294
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:23,759
Couldn't you just stay in Taipei?

295
00:16:24,399 --> 00:16:25,559
To be blunt,

296
00:16:26,159 --> 00:16:27,879
Ronghai is so far across the sea.

297
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:29,879
If you pass out drunk on the street,

298
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:32,000
no one will be there for you.

299
00:16:37,759 --> 00:16:38,480
Let me tell you.

300
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:41,120
As long as you have money,

301
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:42,840
plenty of people will care about you.

302
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:44,000
If you have no money,

303
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:45,759
even a wife would run away.

304
00:16:45,919 --> 00:16:46,320
So whatever.

305
00:16:46,320 --> 00:16:47,679
I'll just focus on making money.

306
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:48,679
Everything else is fake.

307
00:16:48,919 --> 00:16:50,240
Only money is real.

308
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:51,279
What's fake?

309
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:52,919
Everything is fake.

310
00:16:53,759 --> 00:16:55,200
Only money is real.

311
00:16:55,639 --> 00:16:57,360
Leave me more money this time.

312
00:16:57,559 --> 00:16:58,559
I have a good appetite lately.

313
00:16:58,919 --> 00:17:00,279
There's never enough food.

314
00:17:01,039 --> 00:17:02,159
I can't leave you more.

315
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:04,000
Why?

316
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:06,920
In case your girlfriend murders you for cash.

317
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:09,039
Beat it!

318
00:17:25,039 --> 00:17:25,720
For your trouble.

319
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:26,880
What's this?

320
00:17:31,079 --> 00:17:32,279
Thank you for looking after my dad.

321
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:33,519
I'm a volunteer.

322
00:17:33,519 --> 00:17:34,359
I don't take money.

323
00:17:34,839 --> 00:17:35,480
It's free of charge.

324
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:37,680
Yes, I'm religious.

325
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:38,680
I just want to help people.

326
00:17:39,519 --> 00:17:40,039
My apologies.

327
00:17:40,039 --> 00:17:41,240
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

328
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:43,880
Your dad talks about you all the time.

329
00:17:44,119 --> 00:17:45,839
He always says he feels very lonely.

330
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:47,680
Do you often call him...

331
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:48,599
...and snap at him?

332
00:17:53,599 --> 00:17:54,160
Xiaoling.

333
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:01,279
You need to behave.

334
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:02,920
You're only in here because

335
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:03,960
you didn't listen to the doctor.

336
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:05,960
Which room are you assigned to?

337
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:07,039
Aren't you with Lin Zude?

338
00:18:07,039 --> 00:18:09,000
No. The one who just went in is.

339
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:10,640
I thought you were next door.

340
00:18:11,519 --> 00:18:12,680
She's a volunteer too?

341
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,599
How does your assignment system work?

342
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:15,960
It's random.

343
00:18:18,519 --> 00:18:19,759
What if I pay extra?

344
00:18:19,759 --> 00:18:21,480
Can we switch?

345
00:18:21,799 --> 00:18:23,640
Please, I'm a volunteer, not a care worker.

346
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:24,240
Crazy.

347
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:27,119
Don't talk. Listen to me.

348
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:28,720
This is a front line too.

349
00:18:28,799 --> 00:18:29,799
The front line against bacteria.

350
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,200
And I'm the general.

351
00:18:31,640 --> 00:18:32,839
Didn't you serve in the military?

352
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,039
Aren't you going to follow orders?

353
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:35,880
Now, get up and move around.

354
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:37,680
How will you recover if you don't move?

355
00:18:38,759 --> 00:18:40,079
Come on, take it slow.

356
00:18:41,119 --> 00:18:42,160
That's it. Be careful.

357
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:43,279
Straighten your knees.

358
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:44,079
Hold on tight.

359
00:18:44,519 --> 00:18:45,079
That's right.

360
00:18:45,839 --> 00:18:46,720
Walk slowly.

361
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,839
See? You're walking just fine.

362
00:19:16,839 --> 00:19:18,240
Need the water changed? I'll do it.

363
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:18,839
I've got it.

364
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:22,759
Here.

365
00:19:25,599 --> 00:19:26,440
Get straight to the point.

366
00:19:27,559 --> 00:19:28,799
New gear from the Americans.

367
00:19:28,799 --> 00:19:30,319
It passed the technical section's inspection.

368
00:19:30,319 --> 00:19:31,640
Ready to be deployed anytime.

369
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,599
One is wiretapping equipment.

370
00:19:33,839 --> 00:19:35,480
The other is communication gear.

371
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:36,359
Take a look.

372
00:19:36,359 --> 00:19:37,720
How many should our division requisition?

373
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:40,640
My eyes are blurry. Read it to me.

374
00:19:41,119 --> 00:19:42,319
The first is a phone cloner.

375
00:19:42,319 --> 00:19:43,519
It looks a bit like a brick phone.

376
00:19:43,839 --> 00:19:46,000
It captures all nearby phone numbers,

377
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:46,839
clones them,

378
00:19:46,839 --> 00:19:47,759
and lets us use them as our own.

379
00:19:47,759 --> 00:19:48,759
Deployed on the mainland,

380
00:19:48,759 --> 00:19:50,599
it means we won't need fake SIM cards anymore.

381
00:19:50,599 --> 00:19:51,480
No traces left behind.

382
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:54,240
The second is a pinhole camera.

383
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:55,559
The Americans' latest tech.

384
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:56,759
Corridor planters,

385
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:58,759
behind light switches—it's easy to install anywhere.

386
00:19:58,759 --> 00:19:59,519
And completely discreet.

387
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:00,519
More importantly,

388
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:02,839
it can go in bathrooms. It's waterproof.

389
00:20:05,039 --> 00:20:06,400
A pinhole camera.

390
00:20:07,319 --> 00:20:08,759
It's really as tiny as a pinhole.

391
00:20:08,759 --> 00:20:09,759
High-definition video,

392
00:20:09,759 --> 00:20:11,119
and it records audio surveillance too.

393
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:13,400
Compared to the previous generation,

394
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,920
both the audio and video are sharper and clearer.

395
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:16,240
I've already tested it myself.

396
00:20:16,599 --> 00:20:18,680
Ran ten sets continuously for 72 hours,

397
00:20:19,039 --> 00:20:20,000
zero malfunctions.

398
00:20:24,319 --> 00:20:25,200
Good work.

399
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:27,279
Just doing my job, of course.

400
00:20:27,519 --> 00:20:28,440
How is Grandma doing?

401
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:31,720
It's rough.

402
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:34,799
She insisted on growing her own vegetables.

403
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:36,279
Took a fall and fractured her hip.

404
00:20:36,759 --> 00:20:38,200
Falls are the worst for the elderly.

405
00:20:38,559 --> 00:20:39,559
Can't she have surgery?

406
00:20:40,039 --> 00:20:40,920
It's a dilemma.

407
00:20:42,519 --> 00:20:44,720
Without surgery, she'd stay bedridden,

408
00:20:45,559 --> 00:20:46,559
risking an embolism.

409
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,720
Surgery carries its own risks.

410
00:20:49,160 --> 00:20:50,319
At her age,

411
00:20:50,319 --> 00:20:51,839
she might not survive the operating table.

412
00:20:53,599 --> 00:20:54,680
Why don't you head home and get some rest?

413
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:55,599
I can cover for you.

414
00:20:58,519 --> 00:20:59,759
Her own son

415
00:20:59,759 --> 00:21:02,039
is goofing off studying in the US and won't come back.

416
00:21:02,519 --> 00:21:03,880
How could she rely on anyone else?

417
00:21:04,759 --> 00:21:05,480
Here's what you'll do.

418
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:09,079
Requisition two of these pinhole cameras first.

419
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:10,920
I'll give you two addresses

420
00:21:10,920 --> 00:21:11,920
to test them in the field.

421
00:21:12,119 --> 00:21:12,960
I'll arrange it right away.

422
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:13,960
Who's the target?

423
00:21:15,599 --> 00:21:17,160
Every Friday,

424
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:19,599
for three hours.

425
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:21,599
As for the surveillance logs,

426
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:24,160
restrict access to me alone.

427
00:21:24,599 --> 00:21:25,119
Understood.

428
00:21:25,119 --> 00:21:26,759
Yingjia.

429
00:21:28,079 --> 00:21:28,480
You may go.

430
00:21:28,839 --> 00:21:29,160
Yes, sir.

431
00:21:29,680 --> 00:21:30,400
Coming!

432
00:23:26,160 --> 00:23:27,200
Looking for someone?

433
00:23:32,519 --> 00:23:33,680
You're not a thief.

434
00:23:33,799 --> 00:23:35,000
Thieves aren't this bold.

435
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:36,839
Who are you?

436
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:40,680
If you breathe a word about today,

437
00:23:41,279 --> 00:23:43,480
you'll be fired from the university within a week.

438
00:23:45,440 --> 00:23:46,559
The more you threaten me,

439
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:47,720
the guiltier you look.

440
00:23:47,880 --> 00:23:50,039
Your wife will also lose her dental license.

441
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:52,240
That botched tooth extraction three years ago

442
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:53,640
that gave a patient a fatal infection

443
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,599
will be dug up and splashed across the papers.

444
00:23:56,759 --> 00:23:57,720
You're crazy.

445
00:23:58,880 --> 00:24:00,480
Your kid seems to have ADHD.

446
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:02,240
If he gets expelled,

447
00:24:02,519 --> 00:24:04,039
it'll be tough to transfer anywhere.

448
00:24:06,559 --> 00:24:08,039
Out of everyone who rails against the government,

449
00:24:08,319 --> 00:24:09,759
you have the highest blood pressure.

450
00:24:10,039 --> 00:24:11,200
Go get a proper checkup,

451
00:24:11,839 --> 00:24:13,160
live your quiet life.

452
00:24:14,440 --> 00:24:15,240
Wouldn't that be nice?

453
00:24:31,319 --> 00:24:33,319
Personnel here for the annual psych evaluation,

454
00:24:33,759 --> 00:24:35,559
please line up in order for testing.

455
00:24:36,519 --> 00:24:38,200
You only need to answer yes or no.

456
00:24:38,440 --> 00:24:39,240
In the past six months,

457
00:24:39,599 --> 00:24:41,720
have any hostile intelligence agencies approached you?

458
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:42,200
No.

459
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:44,279
Are you currently in a relationship?

460
00:24:44,480 --> 00:24:44,960
No.

461
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:46,440
Have you thought about dating,

462
00:24:46,440 --> 00:24:47,440
or do you have someone in mind?

463
00:24:48,079 --> 00:24:48,599
No.

464
00:24:51,279 --> 00:24:52,400
Is your relationship with your family,

465
00:24:52,720 --> 00:24:54,000
such as with your children,

466
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:54,880
harmonious,

467
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,200
with open and honest communication?

468
00:24:56,200 --> 00:24:56,799
Yes.

469
00:24:57,799 --> 00:24:58,880
Why is it taking so long?

470
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:00,799
Wu Jiali, could you keep quiet?

471
00:25:00,799 --> 00:25:01,880
Don't blame us just because you're nervous.

472
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:03,119
I haven't eaten.

473
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:04,960
My blood sugar might be dropping.

474
00:25:05,119 --> 00:25:05,759
Do you have any candy?

475
00:25:05,759 --> 00:25:06,759
Could you give me a piece?

476
00:25:06,759 --> 00:25:07,519
Over the past year,

477
00:25:07,519 --> 00:25:09,359
has your relationship with your wife and family

478
00:25:09,359 --> 00:25:10,279
been healthy?

479
00:25:10,519 --> 00:25:11,200
We get along great.

480
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:13,200
You only need to answer yes or no.

481
00:25:13,400 --> 00:25:14,079
Yes.

482
00:25:14,440 --> 00:25:15,880
Do you believe you have full control

483
00:25:15,880 --> 00:25:17,319
over your informants and friends?

484
00:25:17,759 --> 00:25:18,400
Yes.

485
00:25:18,759 --> 00:25:20,880
Have you had any doubts or objections

486
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:22,319
regarding the cases you've handled?

487
00:25:23,720 --> 00:25:24,119
Yes.

488
00:25:24,119 --> 00:25:24,960
Specifically,

489
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:27,079
do you question the investigative methods?

490
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:27,960
Yes.

491
00:25:29,759 --> 00:25:30,880
No—I mean, no.

492
00:25:31,839 --> 00:25:34,359
Suppose you were once misunderstood and suspected.

493
00:25:34,359 --> 00:25:35,640
After your name was cleared,

494
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:37,799
would you still suspect others involved in the investigation?

495
00:25:38,799 --> 00:25:39,559
Yes.

496
00:26:16,039 --> 00:26:16,480
Chief,

497
00:26:16,759 --> 00:26:19,000
that Chinese medicine doctor I asked you to find—

498
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:20,000
is he actually reliable?

499
00:26:21,359 --> 00:26:22,559
Supposedly, he's very good.

500
00:26:22,640 --> 00:26:24,400
He said to heat some oil in a pan first,

501
00:26:24,400 --> 00:26:25,519
and then rub it on the bone.

502
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:28,799
It's a fractured hip.

503
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:29,880
And you want to rub it?

504
00:26:30,039 --> 00:26:30,960
Sounds totally unreliable.

505
00:26:31,440 --> 00:26:34,240
Well, Director Lin's wife had bone necrosis,

506
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:35,119
and he was the one who cured her.

507
00:26:35,119 --> 00:26:36,319
Necrosis is one thing,

508
00:26:36,319 --> 00:26:37,720
a fracture is another.

509
00:26:38,559 --> 00:26:39,319
Forget it.

510
00:26:40,240 --> 00:26:41,240
Where are those two tapes?

511
00:26:41,920 --> 00:26:43,480
The ones for testing the pinhole cameras.

512
00:26:44,160 --> 00:26:45,680
The red one is from the residence.

513
00:26:45,799 --> 00:26:47,359
I looked, but there wasn't much to see,

514
00:26:47,359 --> 00:26:48,839
so I transferred it to tape.

515
00:26:52,680 --> 00:26:54,200
This green one is from the bar.

516
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:55,279
You can take a look when you get back.

517
00:27:36,599 --> 00:27:37,319
Sir.

518
00:27:37,880 --> 00:27:40,480
Chen Leyuan, Assistant to the Director of the Intelligence Center,

519
00:27:41,079 --> 00:27:41,960
reporting to you, Sir.

520
00:27:43,599 --> 00:27:45,559
How did you know I was here?

521
00:27:48,079 --> 00:27:49,119
It's an urgent matter

522
00:27:49,799 --> 00:27:51,000
that I had to report in person.

523
00:27:52,279 --> 00:27:54,000
You should report to Division Chief Zhu.

524
00:27:54,759 --> 00:27:55,720
You're bypassing the chain of command.

525
00:28:01,480 --> 00:28:02,480
Zhu Yingjia

526
00:28:03,319 --> 00:28:04,400
is wiretapping you.

527
00:28:05,799 --> 00:28:07,680
I heard from the tapes

528
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:09,839
that you often visit the hot springs here.

529
00:28:12,559 --> 00:28:15,359
Of course, the Americans have another new device,

530
00:28:16,240 --> 00:28:17,599
and I've already installed it in his home.

531
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:09,839
So, besides carousing around,

532
00:29:09,839 --> 00:29:11,319
did he mention you at all?

533
00:29:11,720 --> 00:29:12,759
Just a few words.

534
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:16,039
The higher-ups are planning ahead.

535
00:29:16,839 --> 00:29:18,000
They think my health is failing,

536
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:19,240
so they want to find my replacement.

537
00:29:19,759 --> 00:29:21,680
I'd rather they push you out sooner.

538
00:29:21,920 --> 00:29:23,839
Grow vegetables, drink tea at home—

539
00:29:24,279 --> 00:29:25,559
at least you'd save half your life.

540
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:27,680
Then what about the sleeper agents

541
00:29:27,839 --> 00:29:28,559
planted on the mainland?

542
00:29:29,039 --> 00:29:30,799
Those useless fools in the headquarters,

543
00:29:30,960 --> 00:29:32,400
not one of them knows how to run them properly.

544
00:29:32,400 --> 00:29:33,480
It'll all have been for nothing.

545
00:29:34,599 --> 00:29:35,880
Then one by one,

546
00:29:36,799 --> 00:29:38,279
they'll be dug up by Wu Shenglai.

547
00:29:39,599 --> 00:29:41,200
My whole life's work would be wasted.

548
00:29:41,480 --> 00:29:43,160
I wouldn't even be able to rest in peace.

549
00:29:44,839 --> 00:29:47,160
Mom, sleeping with your eyes open hurts.

550
00:29:47,279 --> 00:29:48,240
When you get to the hospital later,

551
00:29:48,240 --> 00:29:49,519
get some more painkillers prescribed.

552
00:29:53,240 --> 00:29:55,680
Isn't using too much morphine bad for you?

553
00:29:57,039 --> 00:29:58,079
When you're dying,

554
00:29:58,079 --> 00:29:59,519
who cares if it's bad?

555
00:29:59,759 --> 00:30:01,079
Being pain-free is heaven.

556
00:30:01,079 --> 00:30:02,960
Don't let those doctors scare you.

557
00:30:05,519 --> 00:30:07,799
Pack the vegetables and porridge

558
00:30:07,799 --> 00:30:09,200
into my lunchbox.

559
00:30:09,279 --> 00:30:10,799
Bring my blood pressure meds too.

560
00:30:11,799 --> 00:30:13,480
Starting today, I'm going to work out.

561
00:30:14,039 --> 00:30:15,000
Get in good shape,

562
00:30:15,839 --> 00:30:17,440
and outlast those bureaucrats to the end.

563
00:30:35,640 --> 00:30:36,440
Who is it?

564
00:30:38,079 --> 00:30:38,880
Xiao Lin.

565
00:30:39,559 --> 00:30:40,680
An old friend.

566
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:47,839
It's me.

567
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:49,680
I won't cause any trouble,

568
00:30:50,039 --> 00:30:50,960
nor make things hard for you.

569
00:30:50,960 --> 00:30:52,079
Just a couple of words,

570
00:30:52,079 --> 00:30:53,039
and I'll leave right after.

571
00:31:06,400 --> 00:31:07,759
You ignored me that day, too.

572
00:31:08,119 --> 00:31:09,599
Actually, I've been wanting to talk to you.

573
00:31:10,039 --> 00:31:10,559
I was thinking...

574
00:31:10,559 --> 00:31:11,200
One more thing.

575
00:31:17,799 --> 00:31:20,680
Could you ban me?

576
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:25,200
I'll just get straight to the point.

577
00:31:25,720 --> 00:31:27,279
If your department stamps...

578
00:31:27,640 --> 00:31:28,640
...a seal on me,

579
00:31:29,400 --> 00:31:32,359
I'll get the label of being persecuted.

580
00:31:32,960 --> 00:31:34,000
That's really important to me.

581
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:35,799
That foreign money,

582
00:31:36,640 --> 00:31:40,920
like pay for articles criticizing the government,

583
00:31:40,920 --> 00:31:42,119
I could keep raking that in.

584
00:31:45,920 --> 00:31:47,160
Let me tell you.

585
00:31:48,640 --> 00:31:49,960
The university pays too little.

586
00:31:50,440 --> 00:31:53,319
I went into business last year,

587
00:31:53,880 --> 00:31:55,319
only to get hit by the financial crisis.

588
00:31:55,319 --> 00:31:56,440
I lost everything.

589
00:31:56,559 --> 00:31:57,519
Bank interest is so high,

590
00:31:57,519 --> 00:31:58,880
and I have to make money to pay it off.

591
00:31:59,440 --> 00:32:00,920
My old idealism...

592
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:04,000
...has just become a tool to make money now.

593
00:32:08,279 --> 00:32:09,680
I had another baby.

594
00:32:09,759 --> 00:32:10,640
A congenital condition.

595
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:13,079
I have to earn money for the surgery.

596
00:32:16,240 --> 00:32:17,480
I've quit doing that now.

597
00:32:18,200 --> 00:32:20,799
On the mainland, I strictly do business.

598
00:32:21,319 --> 00:32:21,920
I'm sorry.

599
00:32:35,960 --> 00:32:36,640
Xiao Lin.

600
00:32:37,079 --> 00:32:37,880
Anything else?

601
00:32:39,440 --> 00:32:41,000
Is it easy to make money on the mainland?

602
00:32:43,319 --> 00:32:44,799
There's easy money everywhere,

603
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:46,480
and hard money everywhere, too.

604
00:32:47,319 --> 00:32:48,359
It all depends on you.

605
00:32:49,720 --> 00:32:50,319
True.

606
00:33:34,160 --> 00:33:38,480
All bugs require a power source.

607
00:33:38,920 --> 00:33:42,799
That used to be an indisputable fact.

608
00:33:44,440 --> 00:33:46,200
But that's no longer conventional wisdom,

609
00:33:46,480 --> 00:33:47,720
because it no longer applies.

610
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:50,519
The Soviet Union once had a listening device

611
00:33:50,799 --> 00:33:52,039
they called "The Thing."

612
00:33:52,319 --> 00:33:55,680
They hid it inside a wooden plaque.

613
00:33:56,559 --> 00:33:57,440
It was remarkably compact.

614
00:33:57,799 --> 00:34:00,880
A steel needle connected to a membrane.

615
00:34:01,279 --> 00:34:03,920
Whenever someone spoke in the room,

616
00:34:03,920 --> 00:34:05,559
the vibrations from their voices

617
00:34:05,559 --> 00:34:09,280
were converted into vibrations of the needle.

618
00:34:09,280 --> 00:34:11,159
KGB agents outside

619
00:34:11,159 --> 00:34:16,719
monitored the needle with an infrared radar.

620
00:34:16,719 --> 00:34:20,119
That way, they could decipher

621
00:34:20,119 --> 00:34:22,239
what was being said in the room.

622
00:34:22,639 --> 00:34:24,760
And American bugs

623
00:34:24,760 --> 00:34:26,519
have become increasingly compact.

624
00:34:26,760 --> 00:34:28,440
Surveillance equipment

625
00:34:28,440 --> 00:34:30,280
has become even harder to detect.

626
00:34:30,679 --> 00:34:38,639
They're shrinking toward the theoretical limit.

627
00:34:51,440 --> 00:34:53,320
Many people go to the mainland,

628
00:34:53,400 --> 00:34:56,000
but true talents are few and far between.

629
00:34:56,000 --> 00:34:58,119
Those able to stand here today

630
00:34:58,119 --> 00:34:59,800
are the pillars of Taiwan, China.

631
00:35:00,079 --> 00:35:02,079
The grand cross-strait intelligence strategy

632
00:35:02,440 --> 00:35:03,519
rests on you,

633
00:35:03,800 --> 00:35:05,079
Comrade Lin Kanshan.

634
00:35:06,519 --> 00:35:08,480
With the mainland's reform and opening up,

635
00:35:08,480 --> 00:35:10,400
its economy is advancing rapidly.

636
00:35:10,760 --> 00:35:13,440
Opportunities for intelligence abound.

637
00:35:13,440 --> 00:35:15,920
I hope you will take root on the front line,

638
00:35:16,400 --> 00:35:19,280
stay flexible, and maximize your impact.

639
00:35:19,800 --> 00:35:20,559
Yes, sir.

640
00:35:21,400 --> 00:35:23,920
I will dedicate myself entirely,

641
00:35:24,079 --> 00:35:25,480
until my dying day.

642
00:35:37,599 --> 00:35:39,840
Time is like a wheel.

643
00:35:41,360 --> 00:35:43,199
Once it starts turning, you can't catch up.

644
00:35:43,559 --> 00:35:45,920
Four and a half years ago, I drove you to the airport.

645
00:35:46,400 --> 00:35:48,480
Your legs were trembling when you got out of the car.

646
00:35:50,719 --> 00:35:53,280
Do you remember what you told me back then?

647
00:35:56,960 --> 00:36:01,760
"You're a businessman suspected of fraud,

648
00:36:01,960 --> 00:36:05,000
carrying investment funds scammed from Taipei,

649
00:36:05,320 --> 00:36:07,280
joining a business delegation

650
00:36:07,280 --> 00:36:09,599
to scout projects in Minzhong and put down roots."

651
00:36:10,199 --> 00:36:10,920
"What else?"

652
00:36:16,320 --> 00:36:19,119
"If you're exposed and arrested,

653
00:36:19,440 --> 00:36:21,960
the higher-ups will do whatever it takes to save you.

654
00:36:22,760 --> 00:36:24,280
But if it's over personal matters

655
00:36:24,880 --> 00:36:26,800
and you commit a crime on the mainland,

656
00:36:27,280 --> 00:36:28,400
you'll do the time,

657
00:36:28,679 --> 00:36:29,719
or face the firing squad.

658
00:36:30,599 --> 00:36:31,599
Execution or prison,

659
00:36:32,239 --> 00:36:33,719
not even God could save you."

660
00:36:36,039 --> 00:36:37,880
A sharp mind comes with youth.

661
00:36:39,000 --> 00:36:41,079
Repeat your mission for this trip back.

662
00:36:41,480 --> 00:36:42,440
Go to Europe.

663
00:36:43,280 --> 00:36:46,480
For mainland students sent to study abroad,

664
00:36:46,480 --> 00:36:47,599
nurture those who need nurturing,

665
00:36:48,159 --> 00:36:49,320
cultivate those who need cultivating.

666
00:36:49,760 --> 00:36:51,000
Plan ahead.

667
00:36:51,519 --> 00:36:54,039
This work requires the utmost precision.

668
00:36:55,079 --> 00:36:55,920
Go on.

669
00:36:56,280 --> 00:36:57,320
Then return to the mainland.

670
00:36:57,800 --> 00:36:58,760
First to Guangdong,

671
00:36:59,360 --> 00:37:00,280
then to Jiangxi,

672
00:37:00,519 --> 00:37:02,800
and finally head back to Minzhong.

673
00:37:02,960 --> 00:37:03,760
Do business.

674
00:37:04,440 --> 00:37:06,119
Expand the business and make it thrive.

675
00:37:06,360 --> 00:37:07,599
Seize every opportunity

676
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:09,280
to get close to party, military, and state enterprises.

677
00:37:09,599 --> 00:37:11,039
Focus entirely on landing the big fish.

678
00:37:11,440 --> 00:37:13,320
Unless you give the direct order yourself,

679
00:37:13,679 --> 00:37:15,000
I'll never take risks.

680
00:37:18,960 --> 00:37:20,599
Keeping you from taking concrete action

681
00:37:20,920 --> 00:37:24,320
ensures that as long as they lack evidence,

682
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:26,119
they won't move to arrest you.

683
00:37:26,920 --> 00:37:28,159
There's one more thing.

684
00:37:28,320 --> 00:37:30,119
Strictly between you and me.

685
00:37:31,719 --> 00:37:34,480
The Communists planted a mole near me.

686
00:37:35,639 --> 00:37:38,199
So I'll leak some intelligence out.

687
00:37:38,199 --> 00:37:40,639
When needed, corroborate it for me on the mainland.

688
00:37:42,119 --> 00:37:43,119
What do you need me to do?

689
00:37:43,119 --> 00:37:44,199
Wait for my word on the details.

690
00:37:44,679 --> 00:37:45,639
Build your cover steadily.

691
00:37:46,079 --> 00:37:46,960
Work hard and make money.

692
00:37:47,719 --> 00:37:48,760
Safe travels, Boss Lin.

693
00:37:50,679 --> 00:37:51,880
Last time Lee Teng-hui

694
00:37:52,400 --> 00:37:54,599
disclosed intelligence to reporters,

695
00:37:55,719 --> 00:37:58,599
if State Security had caught me on the mainland,

696
00:37:59,360 --> 00:38:00,840
wouldn't my sacrifice have been for nothing?

697
00:38:01,360 --> 00:38:02,760
If it were me,

698
00:38:03,840 --> 00:38:05,639
and I could die on the front line,

699
00:38:06,480 --> 00:38:08,280
my life would have been worth it.

700
00:38:09,800 --> 00:38:12,679
But I won't ask you to feel that way.

701
00:38:13,679 --> 00:38:14,920
Remember what I said:

702
00:38:15,159 --> 00:38:16,480
under no circumstances

703
00:38:17,360 --> 00:38:19,760
should you become the cost in "whatever the cost."

704
00:38:19,760 --> 00:38:21,119
If there's danger, run.

705
00:38:24,159 --> 00:38:25,360
And if I can't run?

706
00:38:25,800 --> 00:38:27,119
Stop with all the "what-ifs."

707
00:38:27,920 --> 00:38:30,199
Aren't you standing right in front of me safe and sound?

708
00:38:38,599 --> 00:38:39,639
Take care of yourself.

709
00:38:40,960 --> 00:38:42,199
Taiwan, China needs you.

710
00:39:08,159 --> 00:39:09,039
Take care.

711
00:39:30,280 --> 00:39:32,519
Nice game. Next time learn from the monkeys,

712
00:39:32,519 --> 00:39:35,480
and jump higher so your feet don't get stepped on.

713
00:39:35,920 --> 00:39:36,519
What?

714
00:39:37,840 --> 00:39:39,599
Are you playing soccer or kicking people?

715
00:39:39,960 --> 00:39:41,039
Shut up if you lost!

716
00:39:42,719 --> 00:39:43,639
Think we're scared of you?

717
00:39:44,519 --> 00:39:45,519
Stop! Stop!

718
00:39:45,880 --> 00:39:46,800
Do you want me to call the police?

719
00:39:55,039 --> 00:39:56,079
Who do you think you're messing with?

720
00:39:56,880 --> 00:39:57,440
Are you all right?

721
00:39:58,559 --> 00:39:59,000
I'm fine.

722
00:39:59,119 --> 00:40:01,800
These foreigners just love picking on Chinese people.

723
00:40:01,960 --> 00:40:03,159
You've got some guts, though.

724
00:40:04,119 --> 00:40:04,639
Thanks, bro. I'm Xiaozhou.

725
00:40:04,639 --> 00:40:05,840
Thanks, bro. I'm Xiaozhou.

726
00:40:06,320 --> 00:40:07,000
What should I call you?

727
00:40:07,000 --> 00:40:08,679
My last name is Lin. Lin Kanshan.

728
00:40:09,800 --> 00:40:10,519
Which "Zhou" is that?

729
00:40:10,800 --> 00:40:11,639
Like in "carving a notch on the boat."

730
00:40:11,880 --> 00:40:12,599
The "zhou" that means boat.

731
00:40:13,159 --> 00:40:14,599
Are you an international student here too?

732
00:40:14,599 --> 00:40:15,400
No, I'm not.

733
00:40:15,960 --> 00:40:17,400
International students are my clients.

734
00:40:17,519 --> 00:40:19,199
I'm in business. I sell drinks.

735
00:40:19,800 --> 00:40:20,880
School mixers and stuff,

736
00:40:20,880 --> 00:40:22,320
I sponsor all the drinks.

737
00:40:23,920 --> 00:40:24,880
You like soccer?

738
00:40:25,360 --> 00:40:26,039
Yeah, I do.

739
00:40:26,559 --> 00:40:28,679
I usually come play here on weekends.

740
00:40:28,679 --> 00:40:29,719
Can we play together sometime?

741
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:30,519
Sure.

742
00:40:30,519 --> 00:40:31,880
I'll head out first, bro.

743
00:40:31,880 --> 00:40:32,320
Thanks.

744
00:40:32,320 --> 00:40:32,760
All right.

745
00:40:34,920 --> 00:40:36,280
Did you drive?

746
00:40:36,719 --> 00:40:37,320
Yeah.

747
00:40:37,679 --> 00:40:38,840
Could you give me a lift, then?

748
00:40:38,840 --> 00:40:41,639
Just drop me off at a nearby subway station.

749
00:40:42,239 --> 00:40:42,840
Sure thing.

750
00:40:46,039 --> 00:40:48,199
I'm really sorry about today, bro.

751
00:40:48,639 --> 00:40:49,719
I was supposed to give you a ride,

752
00:40:49,719 --> 00:40:51,320
didn't expect my car would break down.

753
00:40:52,039 --> 00:40:53,159
Don't worry about it.

754
00:40:53,880 --> 00:40:55,199
Always in a rush every day.

755
00:40:55,559 --> 00:40:56,440
If the car hadn't broken down,

756
00:40:56,559 --> 00:40:58,519
how would we have time to sit down for a good meal?

757
00:40:59,119 --> 00:40:59,920
Eat more.

758
00:40:59,920 --> 00:41:01,400
You just worked out, replenish some energy.

759
00:41:02,719 --> 00:41:03,760
I really am kind of hungry.

760
00:41:03,760 --> 00:41:05,119
Then I won't hold back, bro.

761
00:41:05,119 --> 00:41:05,800
Go ahead, dig in.

762
00:41:09,760 --> 00:41:10,840
Thanks, bro. Thanks.

763
00:41:11,880 --> 00:41:14,719
Your family should be quite well-off.

764
00:41:15,280 --> 00:41:17,079
College professors in the mainland

765
00:41:17,400 --> 00:41:18,519
get pretty good pay.

766
00:41:18,800 --> 00:41:20,000
Why did they buy you

767
00:41:20,320 --> 00:41:21,719
a fourth-hand clunker

768
00:41:21,719 --> 00:41:22,559
that sputters all the time?

769
00:41:24,280 --> 00:41:25,400
Worried I'd go astray, obviously.

770
00:41:25,800 --> 00:41:27,519
They think drugs are everywhere abroad,

771
00:41:27,519 --> 00:41:28,480
and bullets are flying in the streets.

772
00:41:28,760 --> 00:41:30,000
And they still dared to send you abroad?

773
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:31,079
They worry all they want,

774
00:41:31,079 --> 00:41:32,159
but I still came anyway.

775
00:41:33,599 --> 00:41:34,079
Bro,

776
00:41:34,400 --> 00:41:35,599
how did you end up living in Minzhong?

777
00:41:35,599 --> 00:41:36,280
For several years, too.

778
00:41:37,519 --> 00:41:39,119
That's why I said what a coincidence.

779
00:41:39,119 --> 00:41:40,320
It must be fate.

780
00:41:40,519 --> 00:41:41,559
Look at this restaurant.

781
00:41:41,559 --> 00:41:43,199
You come often, and so do I.

782
00:41:43,480 --> 00:41:45,039
Yet we never ran into each other.

783
00:41:45,360 --> 00:41:46,400
Today it's just such a coincidence

784
00:41:46,400 --> 00:41:47,280
that we crossed paths.

785
00:41:47,480 --> 00:41:49,480
We're practically hometown folks.

786
00:41:50,679 --> 00:41:51,400
A toast with tea.

787
00:41:51,639 --> 00:41:53,719
Friends rely on each other abroad. Let's meet often.

788
00:41:53,719 --> 00:41:55,599
It's just that I have an early class tomorrow.

789
00:41:55,679 --> 00:41:57,480
Next time let's find a chance to really drink together.

790
00:41:57,480 --> 00:41:58,079
No problem.

791
00:42:04,480 --> 00:42:05,840
How was the food today?

792
00:42:09,320 --> 00:42:10,800
Good, delicious.

793
00:42:10,800 --> 00:42:11,960
Let me know if you need anything else.

794
00:42:11,960 --> 00:42:12,760
Wait a second.

795
00:42:14,639 --> 00:42:15,840
Take the tip from this.

796
00:42:16,280 --> 00:42:16,639
Thank you.

797
00:42:16,639 --> 00:42:17,280
No, no.

798
00:42:18,320 --> 00:42:19,480
I'll pay my share, bro.

799
00:42:19,960 --> 00:42:20,760
No need, no need.

800
00:42:20,760 --> 00:42:21,360
Listen to me.

801
00:42:22,159 --> 00:42:23,920
You treat next time, then it evens out.

802
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:25,519
All right.

803
00:42:25,519 --> 00:42:26,280
Thanks, bro.

804
00:42:26,440 --> 00:42:27,480
There'll be plenty of chances.

805
00:42:37,119 --> 00:42:38,639
Thanks for today, bro.

806
00:42:38,960 --> 00:42:40,280
Next time's definitely on me.

807
00:42:40,280 --> 00:42:40,960
It's a deal.

808
00:42:40,960 --> 00:42:42,400
No need to be so polite.

809
00:42:42,960 --> 00:42:45,159
I have a friend at an auto repair shop.

810
00:42:45,360 --> 00:42:46,400
If you ever need anything,

811
00:42:46,400 --> 00:42:47,519
just call me anytime.

812
00:42:47,960 --> 00:42:49,440
Sure. Thanks, Brother Shan.

813
00:42:49,440 --> 00:42:50,719
I'm heading out, then.

814
00:42:50,719 --> 00:42:51,159
Okay.

815
00:42:51,480 --> 00:42:52,079
Bye.

816
00:43:08,239 --> 00:43:09,079
I'm Peng Yuchang.

817
00:43:09,079 --> 00:43:10,679
Inviting you to watch the TV series

818
00:43:10,679 --> 00:43:11,519
Confrontation.

819
00:43:11,519 --> 00:43:12,519
This legal representative,

820
00:43:12,519 --> 00:43:13,639
her name is Liu Shangju.

821
00:43:13,639 --> 00:43:15,119
Everyone calls her Sister Xia.

822
00:43:15,119 --> 00:43:16,119
A woman like her

823
00:43:16,119 --> 00:43:18,119
is definitely the ideal candidate for a courier.

824
00:43:18,119 --> 00:43:19,480
As long as we keep a tight watch on her,

825
00:43:19,480 --> 00:43:21,119
the leads will keep pouring in.

826
00:43:21,119 --> 00:43:23,079
Using the same drop point twice in a row...

827
00:43:23,079 --> 00:43:23,880
The Empty Fort Strategy.

828
00:43:23,880 --> 00:43:24,559
They're gambling, too.

829
00:43:24,760 --> 00:43:25,760
In another 28 seconds,

830
00:43:25,760 --> 00:43:27,559
this meeting of ours will be called off.

831
00:43:27,559 --> 00:43:29,760
Attitude matters far more than competence.

832
00:43:29,760 --> 00:43:31,119
Long time no see.

833
00:43:31,119 --> 00:43:32,320
Gone for all these years.

834
00:43:32,320 --> 00:43:33,920
Just last week we were betting

835
00:43:33,920 --> 00:43:35,280
that you'd definitely never come back.

836
00:43:35,280 --> 00:43:38,000
You'll go wherever there's meat to eat.
